      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
